  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (config_021: multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieves 0.591 accuracy, and we've established that multiprofile >> singleprofile and avgpool >> transformer. The largest unexplored design dimension is whether adding image information improves upon this strong RNA-only baseline. Question: Does adding a standard image encoder (resnet50) with simple concatenation fusion to the best-known RNA pipeline yield a meaningful gain over 0.591? Why this experiment: config_024 keeps the three RNA-side choices (multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) fixed at their empirically best values and introduces only one new factor (image via resnet50 + concat), making it the cleanest single-variable test of the multimodal hypothesis. If it exceeds 0.591, we confirm images add complementary signal and can then explore better image encoders/fusion; if it does not, we learn that at least standard image features don't complement this RNA representation, redirecting budget toward RNA-side refinements. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

